Fillets: the rounding round a wall's corner rounded with the ball's own
radius, between two analytic pieces of the stripe, where the face across
the corner is not square to the corner's axis (mitcad#235).

The case: a tab whose top is a cylinder across it (a steep bowl of radius
1.6) and whose corners are rounded with 0.2, its top's outline rounded
with 0.2. Round each corner the ball's centre stays on the corner's axis:
its contact on the top stands at one point while the other sweeps round
the corner, and the rounding there is a piece of the ball's sphere. The
walls' roundings are analytic (a cylinder along a wall parallel to the
top's axis, a torus along one square to it) and end where the ball
reaches the corner; the walk between them took its sections with the
contacts' mid-point in the guide's normal plane (0075). On the steep top
the guide climbs round the corner and its normal planes lean: the
corner's balls fell to guide parameters before the corner's edge, the
walk swept round the corner before the guide reached it and then found
no ball (the balls on the next wall all have their mid-points in one
leaning plane of the edge before), and the stripe failed ("Path
failed"). Where the planes lean less the walk got through.

- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfKPart: in a gap between two pieces of the
  stripe (also the gap across the period's end of a closed spine) whose
  piece before ends, or whose piece after starts, with its contact on an
  edge into a face on a cylinder of the ball's radius whose axis runs
  through the ball's centre, and its other contact inside its face at
  the ball's radius along that face's normal (ChFi3d_StandingBall), the
  rounding round that corner is the piece of the ball's sphere from that
  section to the one where the sweep (the circle about the centre square
  to the axis) reaches the corner face's other edge
  (ChFi3d_StandingBallPiece: its pole at the standing contact, a
  degenerated edge of the blend's face as ChFi3d_ConcaveTurnWedge's; the
  sweep an iso of the corner's cylinder). It reaches up to the next piece
  where that piece starts with the same ball; otherwise the walk takes
  the rest of the gap, from the guide's parameter where its sections put
  that ball (ChFi3d_StandingBallSection).

Nothing else changes: gaps whose ends are no standing ball are walked as
before.

Upstream: new.
